6,"The Cia-Cia language, casually spoken | Wikitongues - YouTubeAustronesian peoples - Wikipedia",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A_A7zRbJpnU,"This video features Ari speaking Cia-Cia. Cia-Cia, also known as Buton or Butonese, is an Austronesian language spoken principally around the city of Baubau ... The Austronesian peoples, sometimes referred to as Austronesian-speaking peoples, [45] are a large collection of peoples who speak Austronesian languages, having settled in Taiwan, maritime Southeast Asia, parts of mainland Southeast Asia, Micronesia, coastal New Guinea, Island Melanesia, Polynesia, and Madagascar. [46][47] They also include indigenous ethnic minorities in Vietnam, Cambodia ... What language do ciatia people use? Today, the Ciatia people use the Latin alphabet exclusively in official documents and in everyday life, and when they do use other languages, they do not use Indonesian, either spoken or written. , there is no use of Hangul or Korean for practical purposes. Who coined the term 'Austronesian'? In 1899, the Austrian linguist and ethnologist Wilhelm Schmidt coined the term ""Austronesian"" (German: austronesisch, from Latin auster, ""south wind""; and Greek νῆσος, ""island"") to refer to the language family. Where is Cia-Cia spoken in Sulawesi? Cia-Cia is spoken in Southeast Sulawesi, south Buton Island, Binongko Island, and Batu Atas Island. According to legend, Cia-Cia speakers on Binongko descend from Butonese troops sent by a Butonese sultan. What are the elements of Austronesian structures? Furthermore, elements of Austronesian structures (as well as society in general) are often referred to in terminologies used for boats and sailing. These include calling elements of structures ""masts"", ""sails"", or ""rudders"", or calling the village leaders ""captains"" or ""steersmen"".",Cia-Cia,Austronesian
7,CIA,https://www.cia.gov/,A career at CIA is unlike any other. We are looking for people from all backgrounds and walks of life to carry out the work of a Nation.,Cia-Cia,Austronesian
